Open Windows PowerShell as Administrator and execute these commands one by one.
Step 1: Check the Windows Security Log
Get-WinEvent -LogName Security -MaxEvents 20

This displays the latest 20 security events.
Step 2: Generate Failed Login Attempts
1. Press Windows + L to lock your laptop.
2. Enter an incorrect password 3 times.
3. Unlock your laptop using the correct password or PIN.
4. Return to PowerShell.
Note: Failed PIN attempts may not generate Event ID 4625. Password-based authentication failures are more suitable for this experiment. Avoid repeated attempts if your account has a lockout policy.
Step 3: Find Failed Login Events (Event ID 4625)
Get-WinEvent -FilterHashtable @{LogName='Security'; Id=4625} -MaxEvents 20

This displays the latest 20 failed login events.

If no matching events exist, PowerShell may display:
No events were found that match the specified selection criteria.

Step 4: Count Failed Login Attempts and Generate an Alert
Copy and execute this complete block:
$events = @(Get-WinEvent -FilterHashtable @{LogName='Security'; Id=4625} -MaxEvents 20 -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue)

$count = $events.Count

Write-Host "Total Failed Login Attempts: $count"

if ($count -ge 3) {
    Write-Host "ALERT: Suspicious Activity Detected!" -ForegroundColor Red
}
else {
    Write-Host "No Suspicious Activity Detected" -ForegroundColor Green
}

Example output:
Total Failed Login Attempts: 3

ALERT: Suspicious Activity Detected!

The actual count depends on your Windows Security log.

This experiment treats three or more failed logins as suspicious, although that threshold alone does not prove malicious activity.
Step 5: Create a Folder for Forensic Evidence
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path "C:\DMF\Exp3" -Force

This creates:
C:\DMF\Exp3

Step 6: Export Failed Login Events to CSV
$events | Select-Object TimeCreated, Id, ProviderName, MachineName, Message | Export-Csv "C:\DMF\Exp3\forensic_events.csv" -NoTypeInformation

The CSV file will be saved at:
C:\DMF\Exp3\forensic_events.csv

Step 7: Verify the Exported CSV File
Import-Csv "C:\DMF\Exp3\forensic_events.csv" | Format-Table -AutoSize

This displays the recorded security events.
